# PMS — UI

**Always read and apply** `.cursor/skills/` **`shadcn`** then **`product-ui-design`** when building or changing UI/UX. Do **not** load `impeccable` / `ui-design-brain` / `ui-craft*` (reserved for `apps/web`).

**Use judgment — don't obey blindly.** Skills are the floor (components, tokens, anti-slop, workflow), not a substitute for the task. Override when the product wins:

| Prefer skills when… | Override when… |
|---------------------|----------------|
| Adding/composing components | No shadcn primitive fits and a small custom piece is clearer (e.g. bottom nav) |
| Tokens, spacing, tell-scan | A rule fights front-desk speed, mobile parity, or this app's shell |
| Anchor + restraint on admin surfaces | Motion/animation helps a rare moment — still frequency-gate daily actions |
| Checklists before ship | A checklist item would make this screen worse; note why and diverge |

If you skip a skill step, say what you skipped and why in the PR/commit mindset — not silent drift.

Do **not** load marketing/landing design skills (`impeccable`, landing recipes) on PMS.

## Responsive — web and mobile

Staff use PMS on **desk monitors and phones/tablets** (check-in on the floor, enrich iCal stubs between guests). Plan **both** from the first layout — not desktop-only with a later mobile pass.

| Concern | Rule |
|---------|------|
| CSS | Mobile-first Tailwind; scale up with `sm:` / `md:` / `lg:` |
| Parity | Core ops stay usable on mobile — simplify layout, don't drop workflows |
| Shell | Desktop: persistent sidebar. Mobile/tablet: drawer or bottom nav — page chrome must not eat half the viewport |
| Touch | Tappable targets ≥44px; inputs ≥16px on mobile (iOS zoom); prefer `Drawer` over wide `Dialog` on narrow screens |
| Dense data | Tables: horizontal scroll with affordance, card/list fallback, or hide columns — never clip critical actions |
| Done | Sanity-check ~375px and ~1280px+; no accidental horizontal scroll |

Skills handle visual register and anti-slop. **Responsive behavior is non-negotiable** even when skills skew desktop-admin.

## Skill workflow (before shipping UI)

| Step | Skill | Action |
|------|-------|--------|
| 1 | `shadcn` | Search/add components first; compose; semantic tokens; `gap-*` not `space-*` |
| 2 | `product-ui-design` | Pick anchor (`Linear-dense` / `Stripe-data`); add `/* anchor: …, diverge: … */` on page/layout files |
| 3 | `product-ui-design` | Tell scan — read `references/ai-tells.md`; optional `scripts/scan-tells.py <path>` |
| 4 | This rule | Responsive pass at ~375px and ~1280px+ |

**Floor defaults:** no route/page transition animation on shell nav (frequency-gated); no decorative glass/blur on chrome; touch targets ≥44px on mobile.

## JSX conditionals

Prefer **`&&`** for show/hide. Do **not** use `condition ? <X /> : null`.

```tsx
// Prefer
{canManageStaff && <StaffSection />}
{description && <p>{description}</p>}

// Avoid
{canManageStaff ? <StaffSection /> : null}
```

Keep `? :` when both branches render real UI (`isActive ? "Active" : "Revoked"`).

- Forms: `useForm` + `zodResolver` + `Controller` + shadcn `<Field />` — see `apps/pms/AGENTS.md`.
- Optimize for front-desk speed, not marketing. Anchor: Linear-dense / Stripe-data admin.

## React Effects (`useEffect`)

Follow [You Might Not Need an Effect](https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect). Effects synchronize with **external** systems (DOM, window listeners, URL, sessionStorage, subscriptions). They are not for deriving UI state or reacting to user actions.

| Need | Do | Don’t |
|------|----|-------|
| Reset dialog/sheet form when opening create vs edit | Remount with `key` (`property?.id ?? "create"`, `open` session id) so RHF defaults apply | `useEffect(() => { if (open) form.reset(…) }, [open, entity])` |
| Clear local UI when dialog closes | Event handler: `onOpenChange(false)` / Cancel — same place as close | Effect watching `open === false` then `setState` / `form.reset` |
| Derived value (filter, label, total) | Compute during render (or `useMemo` if expensive) | `useEffect` + `setState` from props/state |
| Notify parent of child state | Call parent in the **event** that changed it (or lift state / derive) | `useEffect(() => onChange(x), [x])` |
| Keyboard, pointerup, focus, scrollIntoView, debounce timer | Effect (subscribe + cleanup) | — |
| Sync search params / sessionStorage | Effect OK when the source of truth is outside React | — |
| Data fetch for screen | TanStack Query — not raw `useEffect` + `fetch` | — |

`react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` is an error — treat cascading `setState` in Effects as a smell; prefer key remount, render-time calc, or event handlers.

## GET / list loading & errors

For query-backed screens (lists, detail fetches):

| State | UI |
|-------|-----|
| Loading | Prefer **Skeleton** (match layout), not an indefinite blank or spinner-only page |
| Error (page 1 / detail) | Short message + shared [`QueryRetryButton`](../../apps/pms/src/components/query-retry-button.tsx) calling `refetch` |

### Infinite scroll footer

Paginated explorer lists use [`InfiniteListFooter`](../../apps/pms/src/components/infinite-list-footer.tsx) + `react-intersection-observer` (`useInView`). Data rules: [`pms-query.mdc`](pms-query.mdc).

| Footer state | UI |
|--------------|-----|
| Can load more | Sentinel `<div ref={…}>` — when in view → `fetchNextPage` |
| Fetching next | Compact spinner / “Loading more…” |
| Next-page error | **No sentinel.** Message + `QueryRetryButton` → `fetchNextPage` (resume failed page; prevents inView retry loop) |
| No more pages | Empty |

Do not leave failed GETs silent or without a way to retry. Data lifecycle (keys, mutations, toast vs field): [`pms-query.mdc`](pms-query.mdc).
